			"notes": "Tool Pouch information now moves only when its layout overlaps the minimap in both dimensions. Native map bounds include canvas, decoration icons, names and prepared text, fixing unwanted movement beside horizontally offset maps and missed edge-label collisions. Independent information placement and saved offsets remain intact.\n\nVerified with Hotkey Wheel 1.0.7+26.3, original Buildprint 0.1.19+26.x, local Blocktone 0.1.24 and Better Recipe Book: Rebetterered 1.11.7+26.3: 30 native + 30 client-Polymer HUD scenes, 655 + 655 all-four wheel assertions, 1,968 packaged BRBR checks and four connected backpack crafting profiles. Final native/Polymer server crafting passed 198 assertions each. All 13 real installer/archive checks passed. All nine documented Buildprint API areas were reviewed against the exact supported JAR.\n\nInstall Minecraft 26.3, Fabric Loader 0.19.5 and Java 25+. Use the matching suite on participating native clients/server and the exact libraries supplied by the installation ZIP. Its server profile uses Polymer 0.18.2+26.3. Fzzy Config remains an official publisher download through the installer. Wheel, Buildprint, Blocktone and BRBR are separate client installs; Blocktone's release remains local.\n\nOnly the suite and HUD addon advance, to 1.4.4+26.3 and 1.0.11+26.3. Other 18 nested modules/root classes, original developer inputs and dependencies remain unchanged. Previous releases and the paused SSO port are preserved.\n\nFour downloadable assets: README.md, the suite JAR, docs.zip and the installation ZIP. [Release guide](https://github.com/THENATHE/vanilla-plusplus-quality-of-life-suite/blob/v1.4.4%2B26.3/docs/RELEASE_1_4_4.md) and [complete QA record](https://github.com/THENATHE/vanilla-plusplus-quality-of-life-suite/blob/v1.4.4%2B26.3/docs/FOUR_MOD_QA_2026_10_13.md).\n\nSuite SHA-256: `e4663dddf2e176c3d5d7a669f59822dc76286ed28e195cc1a77b1bb1b3e7d269`."
